                "text": "This week, the Financial Services Committee held a hearing on the federal deposit insurance framework.  Missouri represents what makes our banking system great. \n\nOur varied institutions, from community and regional banks all the way up to Global Systemically Important Banks, address the different needs of our community, from a young married couple buying their first home to the entrepreneur who needs a loan to grow his startup. \n\nAny changes to our deposit insurance framework should ensure that the variety and the diversity of our banking system is preserved, so that all customers can access banking that suits their needs and any negative impacts are minimized.  Watch my questioning here.",
